{R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-74979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ef3ca521064f6da0644188ae9fddb10e4eff435763fcd6e23d30abb70831401"} {"question" "q-74979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-74979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\