 the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-110853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ef3ca521064f6da0644188ae9fddb10e4eff435763fcd6e23d30abb70831401"} {"question" "q-110853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-110853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-110853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-35694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ ${a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-35694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -6 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-35694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ef3ca521064f6da0644188ae9fddb10e4eff435763fcd6e23d30abb70831401"} {"question" "q-35694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-35694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}"] ["math" "B={[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-35694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-76327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${a}_{3}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-76327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the RREF matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=-4,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+(-4)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-2)\\cdot (-4)=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-76327" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ef3ca521064f6da0644188ae9fddb10e4eff435763fcd6e23d30abb70831401"} {"question" "q-76327" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-76327" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "8"] ["text" "${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-76327" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-110972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ ${a}_{3},$ and ${a}_{4}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3},$ where ${a}_{4}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{4}=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -29 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-110972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+{x}_{3}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -29 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-9 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}=-29 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 6 & -29 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the reduced matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=-1,$ ${x}_{2}=-2,$ and ${x}_{3}=-3,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+(-2)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+(-3)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ -29 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=(-1)+(-2)+(-3)=-6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-110972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ef3ca521064f6da0644188ae9fddb10e4eff435763fcd6e23d30abb70831401"} {"question" "q-110972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-110972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "3"] ["text" "${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-110972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-76322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${a}_{3}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-76322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 36\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{12}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the RREF matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=3,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n2\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+3\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot 3=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c035526d86ff41eb8875"} {"question" "q-76322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ef3ca521064f6da0644188ae9fddb10e4eff435763fcd6e23d30abb70831401"} {"question" "q-76322" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064318/state.json" "file_sha256" "34151a5639236c16af4187361245fb083bba0831f127c0